---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About Me"
	description="Designer, developer, and creator based in Portugal."
	pubDate={new Date('2024-01-01')}
	heroImage="/blog-placeholder-about.jpg"
>
	<p>
		Hey, I'm <strong>Diogo Martha</strong> — a designer and developer based in Portugal.
		I build things for the web and write about what I learn along the way.
	</p>

	<p>
		My work sits at the intersection of design and engineering. I care about how things
		look and how they work — clean interfaces, fast code, and ideas that are actually useful.
	</p>

	<h2>What I do</h2>

	<p>
		I design and build digital products, mostly for the web. I'm drawn to tools and
		platforms that give people more leverage — whether that's a well-crafted UI, a
		solid API, or a piece of writing that makes something click.
	</p>

	<p>
		Lately I've been spending a lot of time with AI tools, edge computing, and
		thinking about what good human-computer interaction looks like as the tools
		get smarter.
	</p>

	<h2>This site</h2>

	<p>
		This is my corner of the internet. I use it to share writing, experiments,
		and things I find interesting. There's no algorithm here — just stuff I
		actually want to put out into the world.
	</p>

	<p>
		The site is built with <a href="https://astro.build" target="_blank">Astro</a> and
		deployed on <a href="https://workers.cloudflare.com" target="_blank">Cloudflare Workers</a>.
		Fast, simple, and mine.
	</p>

	<h2>Say hi</h2>

	<p>
		You can find me on <a href="https://instagram.com/diogomartha23" target="_blank">Instagram</a>,
		<a href="https://twitter.com/diogomartha23" target="_blank">Twitter</a>, or
		<a href="https://github.com/diogomartha23" target="_blank">GitHub</a>.
		I'm always happy to talk about design, code, or whatever you're building.
	</p>
</Layout>
